==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] spawns after 116.67 seconds<sup>3,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] here can actually be quite the handful without the right [[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha Cats]]; to be more specific, the Imperator Saels have been buffed to the point where they can stack up behind the 1.4M-HP Elizabeths and gradually tear down your defenses. Generally, you want to build up a massive stack of [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cats]] to freeze the Saels and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cats]] to block the Elizabeths' [[Wave Attack]]s, creating a perfect opportunity for [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to show them who's boss without getting harmed.

[[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] attackers like [[Splendid Ganesha (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganesha]] may also help for wiping out the peons and Imperator Saels (obviously, [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]] excels here).

==Trivia==
*Ajillo Highlands is the very first [[Uncanny Legends]] stage to feature no Relic enemies.
*This stage is one of the only two Uncanny Legends stages to feature [[Shibalien]], with the other being [[Speechless Tongues]].

